---
import { sitePath } from "../lib/path.js";
import CopyCommand from "../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import Mark from "../components/Mark.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { FIT_PROMPT, INIT_COMMAND, REPO_URL, RUN_COMMAND, TAGLINE } from "../lib/copy.js";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { resolve } from "node:path";
import type { createExample } from "../../scripts/example.js";
const artifactLabels: Record<string, string> = {
  "charter-input.md": "Original charter", "charter.md": "Charter in the worktree",
  "plan.md": "Plan", "decisions.md": "Decision log", "baseline-checks.json": "Before-run checks",
  "candidate-checks.json": "Candidate checks", "attempts.json": "Run history", "change.diff": "Code diff",
};
const example: ReturnType<typeof createExample> = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve("public/example/view.json"), "utf8"));
---
<Base>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header wrap">
    <a class="wordmark" href={sitePath("/")}  aria-label="Pelaggio home"><Mark class="size-9" />Pelaggio</a>
    <nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#example">An example</a><a href={sitePath("/limitations")} >Limitations</a><a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub ↗</a></nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">From charter to pull request</p>
      <h1>{TAGLINE}</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">Set the direction. Pelaggio carries the work through implementation, checks, and agent review to a pull request. Come back to the change, the reasoning, and the evidence for deciding what ships.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#install">Try one work item <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#example">See what comes back <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <div class="horizon" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><Mark class="horizon-mark" decorative /></div>
      <p class="hero-note">An open-source CLI. Bring the agents you already use.<br /><a href={sitePath("/limitations")} >Read the current limits before your first run.</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="example-section" id="example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="example-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Codex + Grok · Medium work items</p><h2 id="example-title">Two example work items.</h2></div><p>CSV export and resumable import, starting from the same small app. Each has a charter, a model-written plan, and captured execution records.</p></div>
        <fieldset class="scenario-switch"><legend>Choose a work item</legend>{example.scenarios.map(scenario => <label><input type="radio" name="scenario" value={scenario.id} checked={scenario.id === "csv"} />{scenario.label}</label>)}</fieldset>
        {example.scenarios.map(scenario => <article data-scenario={scenario.id} aria-label={scenario.label}>
          <div class="scenario-heading"><h3>{scenario.label}</h3><span class="example-label">Medium scope · {scenario.status}</span></div>
          <div class="work-sheet">
            <div class="request"><span class="index-label">01 / Request → charter</span><p>“{scenario.request}”</p><div class="context-layer"><h4>Already in the repo</h4><p>{scenario.context}</p><h4>Added at chartering</h4><p>{scenario.charter}</p></div><a href={sitePath(`/example/${scenario.charterPath}`)}>Read the original charter ↗</a></div>
            <div class="change"><span class="index-label">02 / The actual plan</span><h3>The implementation plan</h3><p>{scenario.plan}</p><p class="card-note">{scenario.decision}</p><a href={sitePath(`/example/${scenario.id}/plan.md`)}>Read the model’s plan ↗</a><details class="plan-detail"><summary>Open the plan here</summary><pre>{scenario.planText}</pre></details></div>
            <div class="checks"><span class="index-label">03 / Independent checks</span>{scenario.evaluation ? <><ul>{scenario.evaluation.cases.map(check => <li><span class="case-name">{check.name.replace(/^AC-\d+: /, "")}</span><span class:list={["check-result", { "check-skipped": check.result !== "pass" }]}>{check.result}</span></li>)}</ul><p>Recorded against candidate <code>{scenario.revision.slice(0, 8)}</code>. These are checks of this execution; site builds do not rerun the agents.</p><a href={sitePath(`/example/${scenario.id}/candidate-checks.json`)}>Inspect the check results ↗</a></> : <><h3>Results still to come.</h3><p>The baseline demonstrates the missing feature. Independent checks of an implemented candidate have not been captured yet.</p></>}<p><a href={sitePath(`/example/${scenario.id}/baseline-checks.json`)}>See the before-run checks ↗</a></p></div>
            <div class="decision"><span class="index-label">04 / The handoff</span><h3>Run result</h3><p>{scenario.evaluation ? scenario.result : "The charter and plan are recorded. The execution history below shows where the run stopped."}</p><p>{scenario.handoff}</p><a href={sitePath(`/example/${scenario.id}/attempts.json`)}>Follow the execution history ↗</a>
<svg class="joe" viewBox="0 0 120 100" role="img" aria-label="Joe, a pelican at the handoff"><path d="M27 77c-9-15-4-35 9-44 2-18 14-28 29-24 14 4 19 16 15 30l-8 35c-13 13-33 15-45 3Z" fill="#FBF9F2"/><path d="M65 32h48c-3 17-22 23-44 13Z" fill="#E7862A"/><circle cx="66" cy="23" r="3" fill="#071A2E"/><path d="m39 84-3 10m22-12 5 12" stroke="#FBF9F2" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M30 53c8 15 20 18 32 11" fill="none" stroke="#d4ddd7" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="capture-note">Authored demo request and charter choices; real model plan and execution records. These runs use local git delivery. Operator interventions and execution settings stay in the receipts.</p>
          <details class="envelope"><summary>Follow the receipts <span>Charter, plan, checks, and execution ↗</span></summary><div class="envelope-content"><p>This is an editorial reading of a captured execution. Planning decisions are attributed to the plan; test outcomes come from the independent evaluator. A passing check establishes only the behavior it exercises.</p><p>These supervised demos use Codex and Grok. Grok’s unsandboxed fallback was explicitly enabled for this experiment. Environmental containment is not a claim of this demo. <a href={sitePath("/limitations#delivery-records")} >Scope and remaining limits.</a></p><div class="artifact-links">{scenario.artifacts.map(artifact => <a href={sitePath(`/example/${artifact.path}`)}>{artifactLabels[artifact.path.split("/").at(-1)!] ?? artifact.path.split("/").at(-1)}</a>)}<a href={sitePath("/example/receipt.json")} >Capture manifest</a></div><pre>{JSON.stringify({revision:scenario.revision,status:scenario.status,operatorInterventions:example.receipt.operatorInterventions,artifacts:scenario.artifacts},null,2)}</pre></div></details>
        </article>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="working wrap" aria-labelledby="working-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h2 id="working-title">Start with a work item.</h2></div><div class="working-copy"><p>Give the work an outcome, boundaries, and a way to check it. Pelaggio picks it up, plans when the item calls for it, and runs implementation, checks, and review with your configured agents.</p><p>Each item gets a git worktree and branch. Shipping opens a pull request by default. The diff, test results, and review give you something concrete to inspect before landing; your shipping configuration controls that last step.</p><p>Start with a change you can judge yourself. Tests cover what they exercise. Review can miss things. Read the operating limits before your first run.</p><a class="text-link" href={sitePath("/limitations")} >Read the operating limits ↗</a></div></section>

    <section id="install" class="install wrap" aria-labelledby="install-title"><div class="install-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Try it locally</p><h2 id="install-title">Set up your repository.</h2><p>You’ll need Node 20.6+, git, an authenticated agent CLI, and <code>gh</code> for GitHub pull requests. Provider setup varies; <a href={`${REPO_URL}#quickstart`}>check the setup guide</a> first.</p><p><a href={sitePath("/limitations#before-a-run")} >Before you run it ↗</a></p></div><ol class="install-steps"><li><h3>Generate the configuration</h3><p>Generate the skills, quality rubric, sample roadmap, and configuration.</p><CopyCommand command={INIT_COMMAND} /></li><li><h3>Adapt it to your project</h3><p>Give this prompt to your agent. Read the resulting diff before continuing.</p><CopyCommand command={FIT_PROMPT} wrap label="Copy the setup prompt" /></li><li><h3>Run one work item</h3><p>Stay nearby for the first cycle. Follow the work and inspect what comes back.</p><CopyCommand command={RUN_COMMAND} /></li></ol></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer wrap"><div><a class="wordmark" href={sitePath("/")} ><Mark class="size-7" />Pelaggio</a><p>© 2026 Chris Horne</p></div><nav aria-label="Footer"><a href={sitePath("/limitations")} >Limitations</a><a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>AGPL-3.0-or-later</a><a href={REPO_URL}>Source ↗</a></nav></footer>
</Base>
